{"question_id": "195a1a1b", "question_type": "single-session-preference", "response": "Here are some evening activities drawn from your wind-down plan and relaxation options:\n\n**Structured wind-down (targeting sleep by 9:30 pm)**\n- Finish work or stimulating activities by 8:30 pm\n- Start a relaxation technique around 8:45 pm — reading, meditation, or deep breathing\n- Put away electronic devices by 9:15 pm (at least 30 minutes before bed)\n- Prepare your sleep environment around 9:20 pm — make the bed, dim the lights\n- Begin your bedtime routine around 9:25 pm — brush teeth, change into pajamas\n- Lights out by 9:30 pm\n\n**Relaxation / meditation options**\n- Guided sleep meditations: 'Sleep' by Headspace (10 min) — which you found relaxing before — 'Deep Sleep' by Calm (20 min), 'Sleep Meditation' by Andrew Weil (10 min), 'Guided Sleep Meditation' by Meditation Studio (15 min), or 'Sleep Story: The Magical Forest' by Calm (20 min)\n- Relaxation meditations: 'Body Scan' by Insight Timer (10 min) — the one you planned to try tonight — 'Relaxation Response' by Dr. Herbert Benson (10 min), 'Loving-Kindness Meditation' by Jack Kornfield (10 min), 'Progressive Muscle Relaxation' by Meditation Studio (10 min), or 'Rainy Night' by Rainy Mood (10 min)\n- Other calming resources: Andrew Weil's YouTube meditations, Rainy Mood, the Sleep With Me podcast, Meditation Oasis, or UCLA Mindful Awareness Research Center meditations\n\nSince you especially enjoyed the imagery and visualization in Headspace's 'Sleep' meditation, the Calm sleep story and visualization-based body scans are likely to suit you well too.", "n_records": 39, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 4601, "completion_tokens": 1228, "calls": 2}, "selected": ["self|time_management_struggle", "self|project_deadline", "self|time_consuming_tasks", "self|daily_available_hours", "self|productive_times", "self|morning_exercise_routine", "self|schedule_preference", "self|distractions_to_minimize", "self|time_management_tools",